C3  a hash part keeps every marginal witness-free while the joint law is not
  over all 256 public functions H on a 4-element domain:
    witness-dependent MARGINAL  : 0
    witness-dependent JOINT law : 252  (hypothesis (iv) fails on exactly these)
    some chi distinguishes      : 252  (max adaptive TV = 1)

C4/C5  the naive approximate form is FALSE; the identical-until-bad form holds
  |C|=2   per-rho TV=1/2      steering chi: TV=1    Pr[BAD]=1    | constant chi: TV=1/2      Pr[BAD]=1/2      | blow-up x2
  |C|=4   per-rho TV=1/4      steering chi: TV=1    Pr[BAD]=1    | constant chi: TV=1/4      Pr[BAD]=1/4      | blow-up x4
  |C|=8   per-rho TV=1/8      steering chi: TV=1    Pr[BAD]=1    | constant chi: TV=1/8      Pr[BAD]=1/8      | blow-up x8
  |C|=16  per-rho TV=1/16     steering chi: TV=1    Pr[BAD]=1    | constant chi: TV=1/16     Pr[BAD]=1/16     | blow-up x16
  |C|=32  per-rho TV=1/32     steering chi: TV=1    Pr[BAD]=1    | constant chi: TV=1/32     Pr[BAD]=1/32     | blow-up x32
  => per-rho TV is NOT a bound on the adaptive TV: the blow-up is exactly |C|.
  => Pr[BAD] measured in the ADAPTIVE experiment IS a bound, in every row.

C6  one witness-dependent refusal class, steered by a constant challenge function
  |C|=4   worst chi: TV=1      random chi (200 draws): mean TV=0.6575  (2/|C| = 0.5000)
  |C|=8   worst chi: TV=1      random chi (200 draws): mean TV=0.3212  (2/|C| = 0.2500)
  |C|=16  worst chi: TV=1      random chi (200 draws): mean TV=0.1634  (2/|C| = 0.1250)
  => for ARBITRARY chi the conclusion is FALSE whenever one refusal is
     witness-dependent; for an oracle chi the distance is ~1/|C|.

